 "method": "Round 1 = v18_oil exactly (blocks 8, 5, 4). Round 2 = X (2 weeks) + Y (7 weeks) + Z (8 weeks): X+Y is a resolvable minimum covering of K18 by 9 classes whose doubled couples form a 1-factor F', each F' couple once in X and once in Y; Z is round 1's nearly Kirkman triple system relabelled so that its missing 1-factor is F'. X is clash-free against round 1's last 4 weeks, so the five blocks are 8, 5, 4+2, 7, 8 (the optimum: a clash-free run has at most 8 weeks). The covering was found by z3 with a prescribed fixed-point-free order-3 automorphism (X = 2 invariant weeks; Y = a 3-week orbit + 4 invariant weeks, with X + the first 5 weeks of Y clash-free so F' recurs only in Y's last 2 weeks), then relabelled: two couple-disjoint weeks are a cubic bipartite graph on 6+6 trios whose 18 edges are the bowlers, and the 34 admissible week pairs in the complement of round 1's last block (clash-free, one week transversal to the positions the bowlers are owed after 17 weeks) were matched to X by graph isomorphism, keeping the isomorphism with fewest round-1 trios. Z's relabelling by hill-climb (no repeated trio). Lanes of round 2 by z3 (QF_FD) against round 1's counts: every bowler 5 or 6 times on every lane pair over 34 weeks. Positions: round 1 unchanged, week 18 gives each bowler the position they are owed, weeks 19-34 by de Werra edge colouring; within one of even after every week. Prefix spread 2 only at week 25 (and round 1's weeks 9-10); 3 round-2 trios also occur in round 1."
